WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.002
- One use case is

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.004
to use BigQuery
for Preprocessing

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.706
of the training data.

00:00:05.706 --> 00:00:09.476
So the TensorFlow
or the Machine Learning Engine

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.812
or ML Engine itself
is not suited

00:00:11.812 --> 00:00:13.480
for the duty of preprocessing

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.017
or collecting all the data
from Enterprise Systems.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.486
So you can use BigQuery
as a data bank

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.121
so you can gather all the data

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.289
coming from the Enterprise

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:24.658
application server,
with server databases.

00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:29.730
All imported to the BigQuery and
do some preprocessing on that,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.500
then you can add exported data,
other training data

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.502
to the TensorFlow or ML Engine.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.541
So let's take a look at the
actual demonstrations for that.

00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:43.544
Here, I'd like to use
the Cloud Datalab

00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:46.880
to do--to use the BigQuery
for preparation,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.683
or preprocessing
and use the TensorFlow

00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:51.818
to train your Neural Network model

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.754
for machine learning analytics.

00:00:57.758 --> 00:00:59.760
So this is just something
I have prepared

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.962
that is called
Classifying Manhattan.

00:01:01.962 --> 00:01:04.820
Here we are importing the bunch
of the location data

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.701
from BigQuery and trained the
Neural Network model

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:11.140
to classify whether each
location is Manhattan or not.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.409
So...

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.400
We clear all the cells first.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.340
And now let's take a look at
what kind of the training datas

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.918
that we'll be using
by executing this query.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.387
So I'll be using the--

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:30.858
another public data set
called NYPD Collisions.

00:01:30.858 --> 00:01:33.260
That because
all of the car accidents

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.062
happened in the New York City.

00:01:35.062 --> 00:01:39.099
We see timestamp and borough
and latitude and longitude.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:46.373
But you cannot use this raw data
as it is.

00:01:46.373 --> 00:01:48.342
You have to do preprocessing
to that.

00:01:48.342 --> 00:01:50.744
Because you can see that some
rows

00:01:50.744 --> 00:01:52.579
doesn't have any borough data.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.982
Some rows doesn't have latitude
and longitude.

00:01:54.982 --> 00:01:57.351
We have to remove

00:01:57.351 --> 00:01:58.619
useless garbage data.

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:01.121
So again, you can use
the BigQuery

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.490
to do this kind
of the preprocessing.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.326
And also, I want to have
a new program.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:10.330
Is Manhattan --
to have a flag.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:14.501
That flag represents whether
the latitude and longitude

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.204
is inside Manhattan or not.

00:02:17.204 --> 00:02:20.174
So this is the SQL I'll be using
for preprocessing

00:02:20.174 --> 00:02:21.508
and let me execute it.

00:02:23.744 --> 00:02:26.580
And also, you can also
execute another

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.717
called to extract all the data
from BigQuery,

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.053
import it into
the Python.

00:02:33.053 --> 00:02:36.356
So now you have all the data
imported into Python code.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.692
So as you can see, by using
Cloud Datalab,

00:02:38.692 --> 00:02:41.261
you can seamlessly integrate
the BigQuery query

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:43.130
with the Python code you write.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.266
And you can continue use
your scikit-learn

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.936
or the NumPy code
running on BigQuery.

00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:50.137
Sorry about my voice.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.475
So now we have the training data
set.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.177
One is Manhattan.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.813
This could be used as a label
for training,

00:02:59.813 --> 00:03:02.616
whether each location is in
Manhattan or not,

00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:05.786
and pairs of the latitude
and longitude.

00:03:05.786 --> 00:03:07.221
10,000 rows.

00:03:08.155 --> 00:03:10.524
So let's do the feature scaling.

00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:13.126
Before starting training,
usually in machine learning,

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.262
you have to clean the data out.

00:03:15.262 --> 00:03:17.331
Clean out--cleansing of the
data.

00:03:17.331 --> 00:03:22.002
And one important thing there is
to do is feature scaling.

00:03:22.002 --> 00:03:25.038
And if you do the scaling
and plotting the data,

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:28.542
you can see the training data
set would look like this.

00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:31.044
Now everything is centered on...

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.781
The, uh...zero.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.917
But still, you can see the shape
of Manhattan here.

00:03:36.917 --> 00:03:38.185
You can still--

00:03:38.185 --> 00:03:42.623
You can even see there's Central
Park inside the data set.

00:03:44.024 --> 00:03:46.927
So this will be the training
data set for neural network.

00:03:46.927 --> 00:03:49.930
We'll be splitting the data
into training data

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.532
and test data.

00:03:51.532 --> 00:03:54.601
And use TensorFlow to define
your neural network.

00:03:56.503 --> 00:04:00.240
Here I'm using TensorFlow,
especially the so-called high--

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.977
what is that?
High-level API of TensorFlow.

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:07.047
And this is one of the features
we have recently announced

00:04:07.047 --> 00:04:08.982
with TensorFlow 1.0

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.685
where you can just write
a few lines of Python code

00:04:11.685 --> 00:04:13.854
to define neural networks.

00:04:13.854 --> 00:04:17.124
Before that, we had been using
so-called low-level API

00:04:17.124 --> 00:04:20.160
where you have to define all
the competition graph--

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.997
low-level competition graph to
define your own neural networks.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:27.301
But now you can just write a few
lines of code with Python.

00:04:27.301 --> 00:04:30.571
So you can see we are defining
deep neural networks

00:04:30.571 --> 00:04:33.106
with the four hidden layers

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.977
and each hidden layer
has 20 nodes.

00:04:39.613 --> 00:04:41.849
We have the neural networks.

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:44.418
Let's check the current accuracy

00:04:44.418 --> 00:04:47.821
of the neural networks
and how these neural networks

00:04:47.821 --> 00:04:49.756
can classify Manhattan
with that,

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.326
before doing the actual
training.

00:04:52.326 --> 00:04:56.396
So now you'll be seeing the map

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.599
classed by the neural networks.

00:04:58.599 --> 00:05:01.034
So this is how a neural network
thinks

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.804
where the Manhattan is before
training.

00:05:03.804 --> 00:05:06.240
So because this is before
training,

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.511
the neural network
is stupid enough--

00:05:10.511 --> 00:05:12.980
is too stupid to classify
Manhattan.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:15.148
He thinks this is Manhattan.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:18.452
So this is where we have to
train the neural network model.

00:05:18.452 --> 00:05:20.921
The accuracy is 75%.

00:05:20.921 --> 00:05:23.357
So you can write
a full loop

00:05:23.357 --> 00:05:26.593
to repeatedly call the
fit method

00:05:26.593 --> 00:05:29.897
to train the model by using the
training data set.

00:05:29.897 --> 00:05:33.333
So now it should be showing
the--

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:37.771
gradually showing the better
accuracy.

00:05:42.009 --> 00:05:44.678
So you are seeing that neural
network model is trying

00:05:44.678 --> 00:05:47.748
to adjust how to classify
each data points

00:05:47.748 --> 00:05:49.683
to get better result.

00:05:51.785 --> 00:05:55.255
So that network is getting much
smarter and smarter

00:05:55.255 --> 00:05:58.358
as you have saw on the Playground
demonstration.

00:06:00.561 --> 00:06:02.296
Yes, it's getting much, much
better.

00:06:04.264 --> 00:06:06.200
So now training is finish.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.403
We got the 99.8% accuracy.

00:06:09.403 --> 00:06:14.741
And now neural network is trying
to split the Manhattan

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:17.924
and Brooklyn with the very
sophisticated code between them

